/-!
# Area `ZassenhausSuzuki`: recognition of `Sz(2^n)` from `(Q, f)`

This module states the two inputs of the Suzuki case and proves the recognition step.

* `SuzukiCoreProp` — the **family-specific computation** on the abstract side
  (Suzuki 1962, §4–5; Feit 1960 + Higman 1963 + Suzuki 1962 Lemma 6 for the structure of
  `Q`): a simple group with a split rank-one datum `H = Q ⋊ D`, `t` in which `Q` is a
  non-abelian 2-group carries a coordinatisation `e : Q ≃* A(K,θ)` (`K = GF(2^m)`, `m` odd,
  `θ` a Tits endomorphism) under which the book's map `f` is the Suzuki map `τ`.
* `SzModelDatumProp` — the **model half**: for each such `(m,θ)`, the literal model
  `SzModel ((m-1)/2)` (the subgroup of `GL(4, 2^m)` generated by `SzGenerators`, see
  `ChallengeDeps.lean`) is a `ModelRankOneDatum` over the same coordinates
  `A(GF(2^m), θ)`, with `f`-map `τ`.  This is the fragment of area `Models` that the Suzuki
  case consumes (fm1's `Sz/` library).
* `recognize_szModel` — S6 of the lead's design
  (`Work/RankOneUniqueness/_design/QUniqueness.lean`) instantiated at the Suzuki data:
  two data with the same coordinates give `G ≃* SzModel ((m-1)/2)`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

open LeanEval.GroupTheory.Defs
open Submission.Blueprint
open Work.RankOneUniqueness

namespace Work.ZassenhausSuzuki

/-- **The Suzuki core.**  In a finite simple group with a split rank-one configuration
`H = Q ⋊ D`, `t` which is a Zassenhaus configuration (`IsZassenhaus H`) and has non-abelian
2-group `Q`, there are an odd `m ≥ 3`, a Tits endomorphism `θ` of `GF(2ᵐ)` and a
coordinatisation `e : Q ≃* A(GF(2ᵐ), θ)` of the root group by Higman's group such that the
book's map `f` is the Suzuki map `τ` (Suzuki 1962, §4–5; see `IsSuzukiConfiguration`).

This is Suzuki's theorem in coordinates; its proof uses
* Feit 1960 / HB III XI §6 (`Q` is a 2-group — a hypothesis here),
* Baumeister–Grüninger 4.6 and 5.6 (`Q` is a Suzuki 2-group),
* Higman 1963 (`HigmanProp`: `Q ≅ A(n,θ)` with `o(θ)` odd),
* Suzuki 1962, Lemma 6 (the cyclic Hua subgroup is conjugate into `Λ`),
* Suzuki 1962, §4–5 (the computation of `f = τ`, BG §5.16–5.21). -/
def SuzukiCoreProp : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], IsSimpleGroup G →
    ∀ (H Q : Subgroup G) (t : G), IsSplitRankOne H Q t → IsZassenhaus H →
      IsPGroup 2 Q → ¬ IsAbelianSubgroup Q →
      ∃ (m : ℕ) (_ : Odd m) (_ : 3 ≤ m) (θ : GaloisField 2 m ≃+* GaloisField 2 m),
        IsTitsTheta θ ∧ Nonempty (IsSuzukiConfiguration G H Q t (GaloisField 2 m) θ)

/-- **The Suzuki model datum.**  For every odd `m ≥ 3` and every Tits endomorphism `θ` of
`GF(2ᵐ)`, the literal model `SzModel ((m-1)/2)` of `ChallengeDeps.lean`
(`Sz(2^(2·((m-1)/2)+1)) = Sz(2ᵐ)`) carries a model rank-one datum coordinated by
`A(GF(2ᵐ), θ)` whose `f`-map is the Suzuki map `τ`.

This is the piece of area `Models` (fm1's `Sz/` library: the root group of the Borel of
`Sz(q)` is `A(K,θ)` with `K = GF(q)`, and the Weyl involution acts by `τ` — the matrix
identity `t x t = m · t · τ(x)`, verified in `Defs.lean`'s model of `σ`). -/
def SzModelDatumProp : Prop :=
  ∀ (m : ℕ) (_ : Odd m) (_ : 3 ≤ m) (θ : GaloisField 2 m ≃+* GaloisField 2 m),
    IsTitsTheta θ →
    Nonempty (ModelRankOneDatum (SzModel ((m - 1) / 2)) (SzA (GaloisField 2 m) θ)
      (SzA.sigma θ))

/-- **Recognition of the Suzuki model** (S6 of the lead's design, via the delivered
`Work.RankOneUniqueness.recognize` and `Work.RankOneUniqueness.rankOneQUniqueness`).
Given the core (abstract) Suzuki configuration `c` for `(Q, f)` and a model datum `M` over
the same coordinates, `G ≃* SzModel ((m-1)/2)`. -/
theorem recognize_szModel
    {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G] [IsSimpleGroup G] {H Q : Subgroup G} {t : G}
    (hsplit : IsSplitRankOne H Q t)
    {m : ℕ} (θ : GaloisField 2 m ≃+* GaloisField 2 m)
    (M : ModelRankOneDatum (SzModel ((m - 1) / 2)) (SzA (GaloisField 2 m) θ) (SzA.sigma θ))
    (c : IsSuzukiConfiguration G H Q t (GaloisField 2 m) θ) :
    Nonempty (G ≃* SzModel ((m - 1) / 2)) :=
  RankOneUniqueness.recognize RankOneUniqueness.rankOneQUniqueness hsplit M c.e
    (fun _ _ hx hrel => c.frel_eq hx hrel)

end Work.ZassenhausSuzuki
